    THE ANSWER IS INFORMATIVE — the burst carries the word better
    than the babble the same creature produces unprompted.

    'voice' is the nine motor groups plus loudness and voicing.
    'articulators' drops loudness and voicing entirely, so it cannot
    pass on "one word makes it louder" -- it is a claim about two
    SOUNDS rather than two amounts of sound.
    'audible d'' is the bias-corrected cepstral ruler: 1.0 is roughly
    76% correct for a listener.
    'EAR still knows' is the auditory module on the same trials in the
    same window. It is the control that makes this a claim about
    repeating rather than about hearing: in the scored window the
    stimulus is gone from the ear and still present in the voice.

